From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mscoree, d3d11: two debug messages that were not gaps (3620)

mscoree, d3d11: two debug messages that were not gaps

mscoree: the sku attribute of <supportedRuntime> only names the SKU the
program targets (the runtime is chosen by version, which is implemented); the
FIXME becomes a TRACE. d3d11: the values ID3D11Device::CheckFeatureSupport
gives for D3D11_FEATURE_THREADING are driver-dependent on Windows (the test
accepts TRUE or FALSE); the FIXME becomes a TRACE. Browser-facing (d3d11).
---
diff --git a/dlls/d3d11/device.c b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
index 021b151..c64effe 100644
--- a/dlls/d3d11/device.c
+++ b/dlls/d3d11/device.c
@@ -4916,7 +4916,9 @@ static HRESULT STDMETHODCALLTYPE d3d11_device_CheckFeatureSupport(ID3D11Device2
 
             /* We lie about the threading support to make Tomb Raider 2013 and
              * Deus Ex: Human Revolution happy. */
-            FIXME("Returning fake threading support data.\n");
+            /* what drivers report on Windows differs (the test accepts TRUE or FALSE); wined3d serialises
+             * creation through its command stream and command lists are made by this layer */
+            TRACE("Returning threading support data.\n");
             threading_data->DriverConcurrentCreates = TRUE;
             threading_data->DriverCommandLists = TRUE;
             return S_OK;
diff --git a/dlls/mscoree/config.c b/dlls/mscoree/config.c
index 92680ef..b30477a 100644
--- a/dlls/mscoree/config.c
+++ b/dlls/mscoree/config.c
@@ -463,7 +463,7 @@ static HRESULT parse_supported_runtime(ConfigFileHandler *This, ISAXAttributes *
     {
         hr = ISAXAttributes_getValueFromName(pAttr, empty, 0, sku, lstrlenW(sku), &value, &value_size);
         if (SUCCEEDED(hr))
-            FIXME("sku=%s not implemented\n", debugstr_wn(value, value_size));
+            TRACE("sku=%s (informational: the runtime is picked by version)\n", debugstr_wn(value, value_size));
         hr = S_OK;
     }
 
